.com/users/another-ascii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/another-ascii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/another-ascii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/another-ascii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/another-ascii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/another-ascii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/another-ascii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/another-ascii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T13:32:48Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T13:32:48Z","body":"I am able to reproduce the issue on Mac mini M1, 2020, Sequoia 15.5.\n\nI am updating from Godot 4.4.1 to 4.5 beta 3. Enclosed is a minimum reproduction consisting of a shader where I connect all inputs of a visual shader. After the update inputs are not connected in the same way as before the update. I have experienced the issue with alpha scissors but as seen in the attached screenshots it may affect other inputs as well.\n\nUpdating does not seem to result in altered shader files.\n\n### 4.4.1\n<img width=\"723\" height=\"1267\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a8ccf6c-7a34-44b9-b5a9-7d9a53aa16c7\" />\n\n### 4.5 beta 3\n<img width=\"785\" height=\"1316\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0edf394e-847d-479e-94bd-2a73bc685b6f\" />\n\n### Minimal reproducable project\n[test_4_4_1_upd_to_4_5_beta_3.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21183949/test_4_4_1_upd_to_4_5_beta_3.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062362344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]